	(text "Layout Note: \n\nLow-Impedance Power-to-Analog Ground Planes: \nEnsure your PCB layout uses a continuous, low-impedance ground plane underneath the SoC and power stage. \nKeep the distance between the low-side shunt ground return and the STSPIN32G4 ground pins as short and wide \nas possible to minimize $I \\times R$ trace resistance and parasitic inductance ($L \\times di/dt$).\n\nKeep High-Current Paths Away: \nRoute the heavy phase current return paths on your PCB far away from the quiet analog ground traces surrounding the SoC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -119.634 128.778 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 255 4 4 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f1199beb-64c3-4280-add7-d0eb9d9ef914")
	)
	(text "Current Sense U"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.162 110.744 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fd594ebf-8e59-470e-b93e-a1ceb00ff889")
	)
	(text_box "Bootstrap Cap (BOOTx - OUTx)\n\nFor STL110N10F7, since V_GS(th, max) = 4.5V and R_DS(on, max) spec'd at V_GS = 10V, VCC = 10V set in FW\n\nC_BOOT(min) >= (10*Q_g)/V_GS = (10*72nC)/10V = 72nF\n\nBut take 1uF from EVSPIN32G4 for plenty of safety buffer against voltage sag while remaining small enough to fully recharge when GLSx on"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 38.1001 0)
		(size 93.98 20.3199)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10dc809b-c166-4dab-b09a-699ce9b6da8d")
	)
	(text_box "Phase Voltage (=/= BEMF) Sense\n- Both FOC and 6-step require the phase voltages to be measured to find BEMF, thus they CAN use the same hardware for measuring phase voltages\n\n6-step Commutation:\n- With 6-step, zero-crossings are detected EITHER in-software (by sampling the voltage directly with ADC) OR in-hardware (by using a comparator to detect the crossing)\n- This board will only support SOFTWARE-based zero-crossing detection, so the associated pins only require ADCx and not COMPx\n- Note: Virtual Neutral Point could also be determined in either SW or HW, but choosing SW (see Control sheet)\n- C0G/NP0 is a MUST for the capacitors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 144.7801 0)
		(size 78.74 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7b44e567-9a7b-418b-a81a-d93f1003eebf")
	)
	(text_box "PGA Configuration: Inverting Mode (non-inverting disallows DC bias) (AN5306 3.4.1)\n\nVINP (OPP/non-inverting)\n- HW: NC, free up OPAMPx_VINP pins. Might need zero-current offset calibration.\n- FW: VP_SEL[1:0] = 11 to cut off VINP and route internal DAC ch (RM0440 25.3.4)\n\nVINM (OPN/inverting)\n- HW: small R to limit curr (R1_internal=10k => G_error=0.1%)\n- FW: VM_SEL[1:0] = 10 to enable PGA mode (internal feedback R's) (AN5306 3.4.1)\n\nVOUT (OPO)\n- HW: NC, free up pins with OPAMPx_VOUT for other periphs\n- FW: OPAINTOEN = 1 to cut off VOUT and route internal ADC ch (RM0440 25.3.4)\n\nPGA_GAIN[4:0] = 8 to 13 to implement an inverting amplifier (12=>-31, 13=>-63)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 109.159 0)
		(size 86.36 33.0811)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8784e90b-d30e-47a6-a916-52a31b3cc497")
	)
	(text_box "Transfer Function: V_OUT = V_DAC - ( |G_inverting| * V_SHUNT )\n- To keep 0A midpoint at VDD / 2 = 1.65V, config DAC at 2048\n- G=-63 (bench testing): {-26, 26} [A] -> {0.012, 3.288} [V]\n- G=-31 (regular riding): {-53, 53} [A] -> {0.007, 3.293} [V]"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 109.2201 0)
		(size 68.58 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a52eb0f4-67f5-4039-9986-a56bc20aa817")
	)
	(text_box "Asymmetric Gate Drive (GHSx/GLSx - GATE)\n\nTurn-off (gate pulled low) faster due to discharge thru D, so shoot-through avoided. Optional series R to damp voltage spikes in the path.\n\nTurn-on (gate pulled high) slowed by R to reduce voltage spikes\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 20.3201 0)
		(size 93.98 17.7799)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d0eff5b7-bef8-48a7-ab31-f6eeb9fb9502")
	)
	(text_box "External Filtering Resistor: R_f = 10 ohms\nInternal op-amp has high input impedance, so effect on measurement is negligible\n\nExternal Filtering Capacitor: C_f = 1 nF (C0G/NP0 is a MUST)\nSTM32G431C6 datasheet gives GBW_min=7MHz & BW_PGA=GBW/G, so G_worst=-63 => BW_worst=7MHz/64=109kHz > f_FOC=50kHz\nTheoretically fine to DNP a C_f, but add 1nF anyway to prevent high-freq MOSFET switching noise before captured by the ADC\nC_f cannot hurt since f_c=15.91MHz >>> 109kHz=BW_worst"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.38 119.3801 0)
		(size 68.58 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd330900-9cf4-47c6-9eca-12150519a564")
	)
	(text_box "Shunt Resistor\n\nFor a +/-50mV drop at +/-50A, R = 1.0m = 2.0m || 2.0m\n\nPair of parallel resistors, so 50A cts => 2.5W total (> 1.25W each)\n\nAt +/-2A, drop is +/-2mV, but use OPAMP configured in PGA mode (and voltage bias from internal DAC connection) to map to ADC range accordingly (bench testing will use way higher gain than while riding it fr)\n\nReason for not having an external resistor network for current sensing is it would mean a fixed gain, thus it could not be flexible for both bench testing and actually riding\n\nLayout Note: \n- Using just regular 2-pin resistors despite the choice of symbol (4-pin kelvin sense)\n- Use Kelvin (differential trace pair) connections from inner pads to input pins\n\nFW Notes: \n- Implement OCP (5.5.2 in UM2896) all in firmware by routing OPO_x to COMPx's non-inverting input and compared against the corresponding overcurrent threshoold voltage generated by an internal DAC. If an OCP event occurs, the comparator trips the TIM1_BKIN line, which shuts down the gate driver outputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 58.4199 0)
		(size 93.98 48.2601)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e4389e69-24d6-4360-8d21-6851cb2e43b7")
	)
